  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "The number of people attending the yearly Abletown Show is rising by 5% per annum, and the number attending the yearly Bush Creek Show is falling by 5% per annum. In the first year under consideration, 5000 people attended both shows.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the total number attending each show during the first six years, correct to the nearest whole person.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Abletown: $34\\,010$ people; Bush Creek: $26\\,491$ people.",
          "worked": "Abletown: $a=5000$, $r=1.05$, $n=6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}S_6&=\\frac{5000((1.05)^6-1)}{1.05-1}\\\\S_6&=34009.5640625\\\\S_6&\\approx34\\,010\\text{ people}.\\end{align*}$$\nBush Creek: $a=5000$, $r=0.95$, $n=6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}S_6&=\\frac{5000(1-(0.95)^6)}{1-0.95}\\\\S_6&=26490.8109375\\\\S_6&\\approx26\\,491\\text{ people}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the ratio (correct to three significant figures) of the total number attending the Abletown Show over the first 25 years to the total attending the Bush Creek Show?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3.30:1$.",
          "worked": "Abletown:\n$$S_{25}^{A}=\\frac{5000((1.05)^{25}-1)}{0.05}.$$\nBush Creek:\n$$S_{25}^{B}=\\frac{5000(1-(0.95)^{25})}{0.05}.$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{S_{25}^{A}}{S_{25}^{B}}&=\\frac{(1.05)^{25}-1}{1-(0.95)^{25}}\\\\\\frac{S_{25}^{A}}{S_{25}^{B}}&\\approx3.30.\\end{align*}$$\nThe ratio is $3.30:1$, correct to three significant figures.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      }
    ]
  },
